<title>USA: MGE spring wheat sets daily volume record.</title>
<headline>MGE spring wheat sets daily volume record.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Minneapolis Grain Exchange's spring wheat contract broke its all-time daily volume record Wednesday when 38,485,000 bushels traded, the exchange said.</p>
<p>The previous record was set in April.</p>
<p>Traders attributed the activity to the U.S. Department of Agriculture's November crop production report released Tuesday, which reduced the estimate for 1997 world wheat ending stocks.</p>
<p>--Kansas City bureau, 816 561-8671</p>
